          %p For the rest of the article we shall assume the use of dependent product types a la Russell.
          %h3#weak_and_strict_dependent_product_types Weak and strict dependent product types
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %strong weak dependent product types
            are dependent product types for which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation+rules"} computation rules
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            \-conversion) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniqueness+rules"} uniqueness rules
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
